This patch is needed because Chromium forwards compiler warning flags into
`bindgen`, but on Solaris the libclang frontend is not using the same warning
set as the GCC-based V8 compile.

What it does:
- drops `-Werror` for bindgen invocations
- filters warning flags that Solaris libclang rejects
- keeps the normal compiler warning set for the actual C/C++ build

Why it is needed:
- with `DISABLE_CLANG=1`, the V8 build can use the native Solaris GCC toolchain
  successfully, but bindgen still fails early on GCC-specific warning options

--- a/v8-146.4.0/build/rust/gni_impl/filter_clang_args.py
+++ b/v8-146.4.0/build/rust/gni_impl/filter_clang_args.py
@@ -12,19 +12,28 @@
 This function filters them out.
 """
 
+BLOCKLIST = {
+    '-Werror',
+    '-Wno-maybe-uninitialized',
+    '-Wno-packed-not-aligned',
+    '-Wno-class-memaccess',
+}
+
 
 def filter_clang_args(clangargs):
 
   def do_filter(args):
     i = 0
     while i < len(args):
       # Intercept plugin arguments
       if args[i] == '-Xclang':
         i += 1
         if args[i] == '-add-plugin':
           pass
         elif args[i].startswith('-plugin-arg'):
           i += 2
+      elif args[i] in BLOCKLIST:
+        pass
       else:
         yield args[i]
       i += 1
